{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927884-which-of-these-issues-deserve-a-limited-line","id":927884,"title":"Which of these issues deserve a limited line?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-07T18:24:34-07:00","id":927884,"title":"Which of these issues deserve a limited line?","content":"- Non-Iremite Mummies (Immortals Incas and Chinese).<br /> - Changing Breeds.<br /> - Dead Wicked.<br /> - Aliens.<br /> - Lovecraft Mythos (focusing on cultists, deep space, ocean and wilderness places like Antarctica).<br /> - Spirits.<br /> - Angels / Demons like In Nomini.<br /> - Gods.<br /> - Wraith.<br /> - Zombies and Risens.<br /> - Mirrors (Alternate Realities, Travel in Time, Crossovers, rules changes).<br /> - Dark Eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T19:03:30-07:00","id":927897,"title":"","content":"We have more than enough on our plate with the existing lines, especially because many of them are still trapped in first edition and have yet to receive any new supplements. Work on updating the existing ones to the current rules and giving them support before things stretch any thinner with a new line.<br /> <br /> I'd be ecstatic to see another Dark Eras (I dream of it being a yearly project) and a book of Shards might be cool.<br /> <br /> Gods is handled pretty soundly by Scion. Classic angels and demons is already handled by Demon: the Fallen and Inferno, and I'd rather see the unique take done in Demon: the Descent expanded on. Non-Iremite Mummies was already done in Mummy: the Resurrection. Spirits feature heavily in Werewolf and Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T00:17:44-07:00","id":929596,"title":"","content":"I see it like this: Dead Wicked may have up to three books into vampire. As Playable spirits may have a book inside werewolf (spirits that are defiled with a human). Other Types of Mummies can win three books inside Mummy, but if it is really impossible, it is something that needs a limited line (the immortal Chinese and Andean). Wraith, Zombies and Risens can win books within Geist and Mummy. Dark Ages and Mirrors need not just lines but from time to time make supplements would be interesting. Angels and Demons other lines besides the Hell, and the Demon can win one, two or three Blue Books (to include Mara, Ahriman, and versions of the type In nomini and Kult), so do not need a limited line. And Aliens is within the Lovecraft Mythos.<br /> <br /> I then would Changing Breeds (Twelfth Line), Lovecraft Mythos (Thirteenth Line) Gods (Fourteenth Line) and &quot;Immortals Andean and Chinese&quot; (Fifteenth and Last Line).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T01:12:51-07:00","id":929612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927884-which-of-these-issues-deserve-a-limited-line?p=929596#post929596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it like this: Dead Wicked may have up to three books into vampire. As Playable spirits may have a book inside werewolf (spirits that are defiled with a human). Other Types of Mummies can win three books inside Mummy, but if it is really impossible, it is something that needs a limited line (the immortal Chinese and Andean). Wraith, Zombies and Risens can win books within Geist and Mummy. Dark Ages and Mirrors need not just lines but from time to time make supplements would be interesting. Angels and Demons other lines besides the Hell, and the Demon can win one, two or three Blue Books (to include Mara, Ahriman, and versions of the type In nomini and Kult), so do not need a limited line. And Aliens is within the Lovecraft Mythos.<br /> <br /> I then would Changing Breeds (Twelfth Line), Lovecraft Mythos (Thirteenth Line) Gods (Fourteenth Line) and &amp;quot;Immortals Andean and Chinese&amp;quot; (Fifteenth and Last Line).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again; why retread ground covered by oWoD Mummy and Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T01:33:03-07:00","id":929616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927884-which-of-these-issues-deserve-a-limited-line?p=929612#post929612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again; why retread ground covered by oWoD Mummy and Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's just the same creature. You need not be the same theme. Like Apocalypse and Forsaken, Dreaming and Lost and Fallen Descent and are on the same creature but with completely different themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T01:54:46-07:00","id":929619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927884-which-of-these-issues-deserve-a-limited-line#post927884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Non-Iremite Mummies (Immortals Incas and Chinese).<br /> - Aliens.<br /> - Mirrors (Alternate Realities, Travel in Time, Crossovers, rules changes).<br /> - Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take more of any of these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T16:55:42-07:00","id":931075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927884-which-of-these-issues-deserve-a-limited-line#post927884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Changing Breeds.<br /> - Dead Wicked.<br /> - Aliens.<br /> - Lovecraft Mythos (focusing on cultists, deep space, ocean and wilderness places like Antarctica).<br /> - Gods.<br /> - Wraith.<br /> - Zombies and Risen.<br /> - Mirrors (Alternate Realities, Travel in Time, Crossovers, rules changes).<br /> - Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div> A second edition of Changing breeds done right, incorporating stuff from war against the pure and skinchangers would be something I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> Likewise a second edition Wicked Dead or Mirrors would also be things I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> Since I'm assuming you're using risen instead of revenant for some reason, since revenants are ghosts with bodies I'd lump them in with ghosts.<br /> <br /> As for gods, you really should have been more specific. Demigods like scion? Avatars? Minor gods like the god of ramen noodles or lost socks? Could also be combined with the lovecraftian idea. &quot;Good news- You're a demigod! Bad news- Your carnivorous tree siblings will be upset if you don't invite them to family BBQs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}